    "title": "Arrange sentence information",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk1-sentence-roles-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Arrange sentence information",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Subjects come before predicates and objects after their verbs. Noun modifiers precede nouns; time, place and manner usually precede the action. Ordinary adjectives do not require 是.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我的老师今天在学校喝茶。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ de lǎoshī jīntiān zài xuéxiào hē chá 。",
                "meaning": "My teacher drinks tea at school today.",
                "audio": "8254cadc8c9c9cd32927162b02fc792c26aac53383cfe033320f21fdf57062e3"
              },
              {
                "text": "他很忙。",
                "pinyin": "tā hěn máng 。",
                "meaning": "He is busy.",
                "audio": "135da4de5d87033b2f0d0bd2e0554b7974fbc1e15584760ec278f42ea90dc206"
              },
              {
                "text": "我十岁。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ shí suì 。",
                "meaning": "I am ten years old.",
                "audio": "459f03331bc663e8234b47cc426b375471ed0fb823d76abb9327f7ca94c773c8"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
